WEBVTT

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:01.694
Jeff Geerling joins

00:00:01.506 --> 00:00:02.767
the NTP Pool

00:00:02.909 --> 00:00:03.958
and explains what

00:00:03.770 --> 00:00:04.383
running

00:00:04.902 --> 00:00:06.081
Jeff Geerling now

00:00:05.893 --> 00:00:07.248
serves public Stratum

00:00:07.060 --> 00:00:08.109
2 time fed

00:00:07.921 --> 00:00:09.489
by his GNSS-disciplined

00:00:09.301 --> 00:00:10.703
Raspberry Pi Stratum

00:00:10.515 --> 00:00:11.352
1 server

00:00:11.553 --> 00:00:12.354
and lays out

00:00:12.166 --> 00:00:13.333
the commitments before

00:00:13.216 --> 00:00:14.383
anyone else joins

00:00:14.194 --> 00:00:14.866
the pool

00:00:15.406 --> 00:00:16.738
Thus I've finally

00:00:16.550 --> 00:00:17.528
joined the NTP

00:00:17.340 --> 00:00:17.941
Pool

00:00:18.047 --> 00:00:19.203
offering one public

00:00:19.015 --> 00:00:20.311
Stratum 2 NTP

00:00:20.123 --> 00:00:20.913
time server

00:00:21.090 --> 00:00:21.844
which gets its

00:00:21.656 --> 00:00:22.434
time from my

00:00:22.246 --> 00:00:23.306
Stratum 1 time

00:00:23.118 --> 00:00:23.802
server in the

00:00:23.614 --> 00:00:24.332
studio

00:00:24.854 --> 00:00:25.549
If you just

00:00:25.361 --> 00:00:26.092
want to operate

00:00:25.904 --> 00:00:26.658
your own time

00:00:26.470 --> 00:00:27.047
server

00:00:27.095 --> 00:00:27.943
that's fine

00:00:27.967 --> 00:00:29.193
the NTP Pool

00:00:29.005 --> 00:00:29.889
is a shared

00:00:29.701 --> 00:00:30.879
global resource

00:00:31.398 --> 00:00:32.412
Full story on

00:00:32.223 --> 00:00:33.119
the dashboard
